[2026-10-25T02:19:45Z] Matt Parrett: Found at 7469958 before the first edit: three gaps between the library and a runtime value. (1) Nothing loads rt/let-go/lang into the GC runtime; lw_rt.lg reads only rt/wasm/README.md's table. (2) The library does not compile through the backend: `(BigInt. sign mag)` and `.-sign`/`.-mag` reads have no lowering (lw_ext.lg refuses `.-field`), as rt/let-go/lang/README.md says. (3) A fielded library deftype is a map at runtime ({:lw/type tag ...}, driver.lg deftype-forms), so wasm.core sees kind 30 and `map?` would answer true. Decision for PR 1: a wasm-dialect unit declares BigInt and Ratio structs with their own kinds and the =/hash/compare/print/predicate arms (hash per corpus/hash/SPEC.md); the driver gains a registry of runtime-provided types so `->Name`, `Name.` and `(.-f x)` lower to the struct for registered tags only, every other library deftype keeps its map boxing (P7.11 unchanged); rt/let-go/lang/README.md gets its own load-order table that lw_rt.lg reads beside the wasm one, as the list the llvm lane can read too. Native facts for the reader tests: 4/2, -4/2, 4/-2, +4/2, 0/5 read as Ints; 1N, -1N, +1N, 1n as BigInt; 1/0, 1/2/3, 1.5N, 0x10N are syntax errors.
